  "id": "olanzapine",
  "term": "olanzapine",
  "definition": "Olanzapine is an antipsychotic medication that acts on several brain receptor systems, including serotonin, dopamine, muscarinic, histamine H1, and alpha-1 adrenergic receptors. It is used to treat schizophrenia, bipolar disorder, and major depressive disorder, and it may also help reduce chemotherapy-related nausea and vomiting.",
